        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "A standard residential roof replacement in Utah takes 1 to 2 days of active on-site work, though the entire process\u2014from the initial quote and material ordering to final city inspection\u2014spans about 2 to 3 weeks.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "1 to 2 days"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "On-Site Installation Time by Material"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Asphalt Shingles: 1 to 2 days (most common in Utah)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal Roofing: 2 to 5 days"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Flat / Low-Slope Roofing: 2 to 3 days"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Tile or Cedar Shakes: 3 to 8 days (due to heavier weight and complex handling)",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              3,
              4
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Factors That Affect the Timeline in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Weather Conditions: Utah\u2019s unpredictable mountain weather, heavy winter snows, or high spring winds can pause tear-offs or delay scheduled crew days."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Pitch & Complexity: Steep slopes, multiple dormers, or hard-to-reach areas in mountainous regions like Heber City add time for safety setups."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Decking Repairs: If rotted or damaged plywood sheathing is found underneath the old shingles, carpenters need extra time to replace the wood before laying the new system."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Permits and Inspections: Local municipal building departments require a short window for sign-offs."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, share:"
